      "writtenOn": "2021-02-19T04:27:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We think that having an APN dedicated to tethering means that the operator has a pricing plan for tethering and the pricing plan is different from the default APN. If operators allow user to use the same APN whether tethering is on or off, they don\u0027t need such dedicated APN. Therefore, we think it is a problem to continue using DUN APN in this case, and disconnecting and not sharing DUN APN after tethering off is common in Single PDN.\n\nIf there is a use case different from this assumption, I think it should be based on a carrier config but I can\u0027t think of it now. How about creating a carrier config if we should find the problem?",
      "parentUuid": "7403afc9_4c9e4bb3",
